id: SceneFilenameManager
name: ᝯㄝₓ Scene Filename Manager
metadata:
  description: "A file's name is metadata nothing else in Stash remembers: once a file is renamed, by hand or by another tool, the name it had is gone. This plugin keeps a copy of every scene's filenames in a custom field, and can put them back.\n\nArchive Original Filenames, in Settings → Tasks, writes the names of each scene's files, without their extensions, into the custom field named below, wherever a file's name is not there yet. A name already archived is never overwritten, so the field keeps the first name the plugin saw; delete the field on a scene and the next run archives it again under its current names.\n\nRestore Original Filenames renames every file back to its archived name, keeping the file's current extension and its folder, wherever the two differ. A file whose archived name could not be a filename is listed as skipped rather than renamed, and a name already taken in the folder fails for that file alone.\n\nRename Files From Metadata renames the primary file of every scene - every file, when the template has an index - to the name the Rename Template below builds from its title, date, performers, tags, rating, resolution and more, with the variant set's base title and partial postfix when ᝯㄝₓ Scene Variants is installed. A filename not archived yet is archived first, so Restore can always put it back.\n\nWhen a file is reassigned to another scene, or scenes are merged, the archived names of the files moved are offered to the scene they went to.\n\nEvery task lists every file it would touch before anything is written, write nothing until you press Proceed, and Undo reverses what the dialog wrote while it stays open. With ᝯㄝₓ Custom Fields Bulk Editor installed, the field is given a description there.\n\nRequires Stash 0.31.0 or newer: a scene's custom fields are where the name is kept."
version: 1.0.0
